{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 12630,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In our universe, when you change from a non-moving\nperspective to a moving one, or vice versa,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17480,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that change of perspective is represented\nby a what's called Lorentz transformation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21360,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is a kind of squeeze-stretch rotation\nof spacetime that I've mechanically implemented"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25450,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with this spacetime globe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27180,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A quick reminder - spacetime diagrams plot\nposition on the horizontal axis and time on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32220,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the vertical axis, and something moving as\ntime passes traces out a path through spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37180,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called a worldline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38180,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the first things you might notice about\nLorentz transformations is that events that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41890,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were at different places at the same time\nbefore the transformation aren't at the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46390,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time after the transformation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48810,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that from the perspectives of people\ngoing different speeds, simultaneous events"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52880,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for one person won't be simultaneous for the\nother, and vice versa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56520,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if from my perspective these\ntwo boxes spontaneously combust at the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61170,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time, and you're moving at a third the speed\nof light to my right, then from your perspective,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65750,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is, the perpective from which you're\nnot moving so your worldline is purely vertical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69830,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from your perspective the box on the right\nwill combust first, and the box on the left"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73810,
    "dDurationMs": 1690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will combust second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75500,
    "dDurationMs": 4299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The takeaway here is that our universe has\nneither an absolute notion of time nor an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79799,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absolute sense of simultaneous events, and\nthat simultaneity breaks down more the farther"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84619,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from each other two things are – a\nbox even farther to the left that from my"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88439,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perspective simultaneously spontaneously combusts\nwith the others will, from your moving perspective,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94009,
    "dDurationMs": 2801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be even farther out of sync with the box on\nthe right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96810,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is described by the time part of the\nLorentz Transformation equations, the part"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101039,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that says t new = gamma times t minus v times\nx over c squared)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106609,
    "dDurationMs": 3991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of the x in there, the farther away\nan event is from you, the more its time from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110600,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the new perspective will be out of sync with\nevents closer to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113810,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though because of the factor of c squared\nin the denominator, which is huge, it's hard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118039,
    "dDurationMs": 3771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to notice anything being out of sync until\neither your speed or distance to the object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121810,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in question are really really really big – like,\nyou'd have to be going half the speed of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125439,
    "dDurationMs": 3781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and be comparing things farther apart than\nthe earth and moon before things would become"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129220,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than 1 second out of sync."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130990,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in that case, events that were simultaneous\nfrom my perspective really would be out of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134830,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sync for you!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136330,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As surprising as this may seem, it might feel\nmore familiar and comfortable when you remember"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140230,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this “getting out of alignment” phenomenon\nhappens to points at the same place in space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144430,
    "dDurationMs": 2161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too, which is literally what we think of as\ndefining motion – from my perspective, this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146591,
    "dDurationMs": 3969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "box is at the same position at different times\n– that is, it's not moving; maybe, “simulspacious”–"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150560,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but from your moving perspective it's at different\npositions at different times – it is moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155790,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relativity of simultaneity is just the other\nside of the coin – the fact that events"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160480,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that happen at the same time at different\nspatial positions happen at different times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164810,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when viewed from a moving perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166810,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All together, in our universe, the takeaway\nis this: events that were previously either"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170860,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all at the same place or all at the same time\nget out of alignment with each other when"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175490,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you change to a moving perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177670,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big thanks again to Mark Rober for making\nthe spacetime globe a reality, and to dive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183640,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more into the details of relativity of simultaneity,\nI highly recommend heading over to Brilliant.org's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188870,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "course on special relativity that they've\nbeen developing simultaneously with this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "series (well, at least, simultaneous from\nmy perspective)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195960,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There, you can explore custom scenarios and\ndo actual puzzles and problems that help you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200580,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "build on what you learned in this video, like\nfiguring out how laser tag would work at relativistic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205230,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speeds!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206230,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The special relativity questions on Brilliant.org\nare specifically designed to help you go deeper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210190,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the topics I'm including in this series,\nand you can get 20% off of a Brilliant subscription"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214430,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by going to Brilliant.org/minutephysics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216510,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, that’s Brilliant.org/minutephysics\nwhich gets you 20% off premium access to all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221710,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Brilliant's courses and puzzles, and lets\nBrilliant know you came from here."
    } ]
  } ]
}
